(vector (map (:db/id -1),
  (:adr/id "2607242200"),
  (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger -> cloud-itonami-isic-6492 disbursement wiring: intake-only cross-actor call, self-mint identity, human-approval resume endpoint"),
  (:adr/status :accepted),
  (:adr/date "2026-07-24"),
  (:adr/doc_type "adr"),
  (:adr/source-format "edn"),
  (:adr/related (vector "2607241800-cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger-actor-blueprint"
                "cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger/docs/adr/0002-http-edge-live-registry-verification.md"
                "cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger/docs/adr/0003-isic6492-wiring-and-approval-resume.md"
                "cloud-itonami-isic-6492/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md"
                "cloud-itonami-isic-6492/docs/adr/0002-http-edge-loan-intake.md"
                "gftdcojp/cloud-itonami/docs/adr/0013-open-business-self-registration.md")),
  (:adr/independent-governance-invariant "isic-6492's real loan lifecycle is 5 stages (:application/intake -> :jurisdiction/assess -> :creditworthiness/screen -> :loan/approve -> :loan/disburse); per credit.phase only :application/intake is ever auto-eligible, the other 4 always require isic-6492's OWN human approval via its OWN Governor. commitment-ledger's new edge layer therefore NEVER drives isic-6492 past intake -- doing so would bypass isic-6492's independent governance, violating this fleet's core 'no actor trusts another self-report / independent governance' invariant. isic-6492's new HTTP surface structurally cannot reach :jurisdiction/assess, :creditworthiness/screen, :loan/approve, or :loan/disburse -- there is no code path in credit.edge.loan-endpoints that touches them."),
  (:adr/two-discovered-prerequisites "(1) isic-6492's 5-stage lifecycle with only :application/intake auto-eligible was not surfaced in the original 2-option task framing -- discovered while designing the edge exposure, resolved by scoping isic-6492's new HTTP surface to intake+read only (cloud-itonami-isic-6492 ADR-0002). (2) commitment-ledger's :commitment/record ALWAYS escalates to :request-approval and never auto-commits (commitledger.phase's permanent structural invariant) -- but V2 shipped with NO endpoint to resume/approve that interrupted run (ADR-0002 there, Decision 6, explicitly deferred). Without building that resume endpoint, any isic-6492-calling code in operation.cljc's :commit node would be unreachable from the live HTTP service, only reachable in unit tests constructing an already-approved context directly -- so the human-approval resume endpoint (POST /api/commitment/{id}/approve) was a genuine prerequisite for this wiring, not optional scope, per cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger ADR-0003."),
  (:adr/self-mint-identity "commitledger.edge.cacao-mint (ported from gftdcojp/cloud-itonami's cloud_itonami.edge.cacao-mint) is this actor's FIRST self-mint OUTBOUND identity -- ADR-0002 there explicitly scoped V2 to need none (the registry lookup is public/unauthenticated). scripts/generate-actor-identity.cljs (an nbb script, per this workspace's runtime-priority rule) generated the Ed25519 keypair ONCE, offline, printing the did:key and exportable private-key material to stdout, never written into any committed file. Private key material stored as the COMMITMENT_LEDGER_ACTOR_SEED Cloudflare Pages secret; the did (public information) as the plain COMMITMENT_LEDGER_ACTOR_DID var. Empirically confirmed (2026-07-24, Node v26.3.0 WebCrypto, both under nbb and via a dedicated isolated smoke test) that Ed25519 PRIVATE key raw-format export/import is unsupported on this runtime family -- only public keys support raw; JWK reconstruction from the stored seed + did-derived public component works and is what commitledger.edge.isic6492-client/import-signing-key does at request time."),
  (:adr/fire-and-forget-boundary "commitledger.operation's :commit node calls the injected Isic6492Client AFTER store/commit-record! succeeds, ONLY when (:op request) is :commitment/record (never :commitment/tranche-release -- only the initial record triggers a NEW isic-6492 intake). The call NEVER rolls back or fails the commit -- Isic6492Client's -intake-loan-application never throws/rejects, always resolving to {:ok? bool :id str|nil :error str|nil}, mirroring Lookup/CacaoVerifier's own exception-safety contract. The outcome is recorded as a new audit-ledger fact ({:t :isic6492-intake-attempted :outcome :ok|:failed :detail ...}), never silently swallowed. commitledger.edge.isic6492-client/->intake-payload sends ONLY principal/jurisdiction/borrower-org-repo/purpose -- never personal-pledge or other commitment-ledger-specific fields isic-6492 has no schema for."),
  (:adr/checkpoint-persistence-for-resume "commitledger.edge.kv-checkpoint mirrors commitledger.edge.kv-store's own load-store/save-store! pattern applied to langgraph.checkpoint/Checkpointer instead of the Store protocol -- Checkpointer's -put!/-get-latest are synchronous (called inside langgraph.graph/run-loop's superstep reduce), so a Checkpointer cannot proxy real async Cloudflare KV calls directly; load-checkpointer asynchronously fetches the persisted checkpoint then hands back a synchronous in-memory Checkpointer for THIS request, save-checkpoint! persists it back afterward. Serialization is pr-str/edn-read-string of the whole checkpoint map, mirroring langgraph.checkpoint/datomic-checkpointer's own existing precedent exactly, not a bespoke JSON codec. This is what makes POST /api/commitment/{id}/approve able to resume a run that interrupted in an EARLIER, separate stateless HTTP request."),
  (:adr/isic6492-client-wiring-bug-found-and-fixed "a real bug found live (not merely designed around in advance): because :commitment/record always escalates on its first run, the graph never reaches :commit during record-core!'s initial call -- :commit is reached only on approve-core!'s RESUME. Each op/build call constructs a fresh graph with fresh node closures, so isic6492-opts had to be threaded into approve-core!'s OWN op/build call, not (only) record-core!'s -- an isic6492-client injected only into record-core!'s never-reaches-:commit call would never fire. Fixed and regression-tested (commitment_endpoints_test.cljc's approve-true-fires-the-isic6492-client-because-commit-only-happens-on-resume) before the final live proof."),
  (:adr/four-preexisting-v2-bugs-discovered-and-fixed "discovered while proving the full E2E flow live (this task's own explicit 'prove it end-to-end for real' requirement), not part of this ADR's original design scope. (1) commitledger.edge.registrylookup/check-registration passed a bare keyword as a .then callback -- confirmed empirically this does not reliably unwrap the map on the REAL shadow-cljs :release-compiled deployed artifact, meaning check 13 held every :commitment/record unconditionally, live; fixed with an explicit fn wrapper. (2) intake-core!'s registry lookup queried the URL path's org/repo, which are structurally ALWAYS nil on commitment-ledger's actual deployed routing (no [org]/[repo] path segments exist anywhere in functions/api/commitment/) -- meant check 13 could never match a real self-registered tenant; fixed by deriving the lookup's org/repo from the application's OWN claimed :borrower-org-repo field instead (the CACAO resource-scope check itself is unchanged). (3) parse-intake-body never converted the wire JSON's nested lender/personalPledge objects into the namespaced-keyword/kebab-case shape the rest of the actor expects -- :lender/id was always nil for any real HTTP caller, unconditionally rejecting every live :commitment/record caller; fixed by reusing the already-written commitledger.edge.kv-codec/json->lender and json->pledge converters. (4) a path-segment id param containing an encoded slash (%2F) is not decoded by Cloudflare Pages' router (unlike a query-string value) -- since gen-id prefixes every id with {org}/{repo}- and org/repo are always empty (bug 2's root cause), every application id in practice starts with a literal /, so GET /api/commitment/{id} and the new approve endpoint could never resolve any real id via their path param; fixed with an explicit js/decodeURIComponent. None of these four fixes touch, reorder, or renumber any of the 13 commitledger.governor checks or the 5 credit.governor checks, and none changes CACAO authorization/security semantics."),
  (:adr/deploy-bootstrap-sequence "(1) isic-6492's edge layer deployed to a NEW Cloudflare Pages project (cloud-itonami-isic-6492) with a NEW, dedicated KV namespace (ISIC6492_LOAN_KV), initial KNOWN_CALLER_DIDS empty. (2) scripts/generate-actor-identity.cljs run for real, captured did:key:z6MksdBBMCXDAZs4PQRyLTzRJpr88FjiayxPrNKfhGwshPLx. (3) isic-6492's KNOWN_CALLER_DIDS secret set to that did, isic-6492 redeployed. (4) commitment-ledger's COMMITMENT_LEDGER_ACTOR_SEED secret set (the corresponding private key material) and COMMITMENT_LEDGER_ACTOR_DID/ISIC6492_BASE_URL vars configured, commitment-ledger redeployed (redeployed 6 times total across this ADR's bug fixes before the final proof passed)."),
  (:adr/live-e2e-proof "curl against the two LIVE production deployments, using throwaway test identities minted with commitledger.edge.cacao-mint and a real self-registered test tenant (e2eproof/commitledgertest, created for real via gftdcojp/cloud-itonami's own ADR-0013 POST /api/{org}/{repo}/register flow). POST /api/commitment/intake -> 201 borrowerRegistrationVerified:true. POST /api/commitment/record?id=... -> 202 disposition:request-approval. POST /api/commitment/{id}/approve -> 200 disposition:commit. GET /api/commitment/{id} -> 200 status:committed. wrangler pages deployment tail on the live production deployment, captured during the approve call, showed the fire-and-forget isic6492-client logging {\"ok?\": true, \"id\": \"loan-8c78r09n\"}. Independently confirmed via GET https://cloud-itonami-isic-6492.pages.dev/api/loan/loan-8c78r09n (CACAO minted with commitment-ledger's own REAL deployed identity) -> 200, application present with purpose field matching the ORIGINAL commitment-ledger intake body exactly -- proving the real data flowed through the real wiring end to end, not a simulation."),
  (:adr/test-status "cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger: 131 tests / 399 assertions (up from the pre-existing 107/338), 0 failures, clj-kondo clean. cloud-itonami-isic-6492: 82 tests / 713 assertions (up from the pre-existing suite, including the JVM-only wasm.*/kototama suite, all passing unmodified), 0 failures, clj-kondo clean."),
  (:adr/west-pin-bookkeeping "manifest/west.yml pins advanced via nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger (8ab8daa46b52 -> 049775c914ee, fast-forward, server-side pin-verified) and --entry cloud-itonami-isic-6492 (c6d963086569 -> ed28aff3cdf0, fast-forward, server-side pin-verified) -- two minimal single-entry diffs, no wholesale regen. manifest/repos.edn unchanged (both entries were already registered, this is a pin-advance only, not a new registration)."),
  (:adr/body "# ADR-2607242200: cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger -> cloud-itonami-isic-6492 disbursement wiring\n\n- Status: Accepted (2026-07-24)\n- Related: `2607241800-cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger-actor-blueprint.edn` (the original fleet-registration ADR for commitment-ledger); `cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger/docs/adr/0002-http-edge-live-registry-verification.md` (V2, which this wiring is V3 on top of); `cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger/docs/adr/0003-isic6492-wiring-and-approval-resume.md` (the full repo-level design record for commitment-ledger's half of this wiring); `cloud-itonami-isic-6492/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md` + `docs/adr/0002-http-edge-loan-intake.md` (the full repo-level design record for isic-6492's half); `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami/docs/adr/0013-open-business-self-registration.md` (the self-registration flow this ADR's own E2E proof used to create a real test tenant)\n\n## Context\n\ncommitment-ledger's own README already named the design boundary: this actor does NOT move money itself, actual disbursement is delegated to `cloud-itonami-isic-6492`/`cloud-itonami-isic-6419`/external rails. Until this ADR that delegation was prose only -- no code ever called out to isic-6492. Separately, isic-6492 (`credit.*`) was a pure library with no HTTP exposure at all. This ADR wires the two actors together for real: commitment-ledger gets a self-mint outbound identity and fires a fire-and-forget intake call to isic-6492 after a `:commitment/record` commits; isic-6492 gets a narrow, intake-only, read-only HTTP edge layer to receive it.\n\nTwo prerequisites, discovered during design rather than known up front from the original 2-option task framing, are recorded in `:adr/two-discovered-prerequisites` above and drove the actual shape of both repos' changes -- most importantly, that this wiring must never let commitment-ledger auto-drive isic-6492 past intake, and that commitment-ledger needed a human-approval resume endpoint it did not previously have for the wiring to be reachable from the live service at all.\n\n## Decision\n\nSee the structured attributes on this entity for the full decision record: `:adr/independent-governance-invariant` (why isic-6492's HTTP surface is intake+read only, by construction, never `:jurisdiction/assess`/`:creditworthiness/screen`/`:loan/approve`/`:loan/disburse`), `:adr/self-mint-identity` (commitment-ledger's new outbound CACAO identity, generated once offline via nbb, stored as a Cloudflare secret, and the empirically-discovered Ed25519 raw-vs-JWK key-format constraint), `:adr/fire-and-forget-boundary` (the isic-6492 call never rolls back commitment-ledger's own commit; failures are recorded, never swallowed), `:adr/checkpoint-persistence-for-resume` (the KV-backed Checkpointer seam that makes the new approve endpoint able to resume a run that interrupted in an earlier stateless request), and `:adr/isic6492-client-wiring-bug-found-and-fixed` (a real bug in this task's own new code, found and fixed before the final live proof: the isic-6492 client had to be threaded into the RESUME call site, not the initial escalating one, since `:commitment/record` never reaches `:commit` on its first run).\n\n`:adr/four-preexisting-v2-bugs-discovered-and-fixed` records four bugs in the ALREADY-LIVE V2 commitment-ledger service, unrelated to this ADR's original design scope, discovered specifically because this task required a genuine live end-to-end proof rather than trusting the existing (JVM-only, test-fixture-shaped) test suite's passing status as sufficient evidence the service worked for a real caller. Each is a narrow, additive, obviously-correct plumbing fix; none touches, reorders, or renumbers any Governor check in either repo, and none changes CACAO authorization/security semantics.\n\n`:adr/deploy-bootstrap-sequence` and `:adr/live-e2e-proof` record the exact bootstrap order and the real curl/tail transcript proving a real committed commitment-ledger application produced a real, independently-verified application on isic-6492's live service.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- (+) A committed loan-based commitment now creates a real, independently-governed disbursement-side application on isic-6492's own books, closing the gap between commitment-ledger's own README promise and its actual code.\n- (+) isic-6492's independent governance is structurally preserved -- no code path anywhere in this wiring can drive it past intake.\n- (+) commitment-ledger's V2-deferred human-approval resume endpoint is now built, and four real production bugs in the already-live V2 service are fixed, discovered and closed as a direct consequence of insisting on a genuine (not simulated) live proof.\n- (-) The isic-6492 call remains fire-and-forget; a real failure is recorded in commitment-ledger's own audit ledger but not surfaced synchronously to the HTTP caller of `/approve` -- a deliberate trade-off, not an oversight (see commitment-ledger's own ADR-0003 Decision 2).\n- (-) `commitledger.edge.kv-checkpoint/load-checkpointer` is not a `ClaimableCheckpointer` -- a real concurrent-resume race across two simultaneous `/approve` calls for the same id is not closed here, a known documented gap for a future pass.\n- (-) `commitledger.operation` now depends on `commitledger.edge.isic6492-client`/`commitledger.edge.pcompat` -- the one intentional, task-scoped exception to that repo's usual core/edge layering.\n\n## Verification\n\nSee `:adr/test-status`, `:adr/west-pin-bookkeeping`, and `:adr/live-e2e-proof` above for the full record.\n\n## References\n\n- `cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger/docs/adr/0003-isic6492-wiring-and-approval-resume.md`\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-6492/docs/adr/0002-http-edge-loan-intake.md`\n- https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger\n- https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6492\n- https://cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger.pages.dev\n- https://cloud-itonami-isic-6492.pages.dev\n")))
